<body>
    <h1>Boot Menu in IGEL OS 12</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p local-id=3D"8681b1e439d2">
<style>[data-colorid=3Dbrq0eho2zs]{color:#000c34} html[data-color-mode=3Dda=
rk] [data-colorid=3Dbrq0eho2zs]{color:#cbd7ff}[data-colorid=3Dbg9h8xzui6]{c=
olor:#000c34} html[data-color-mode=3Ddark] [data-colorid=3Dbg9h8xzui6]{colo=
r:#cbd7ff}[data-colorid=3Dlgxzoavn1p]{color:#000c34} html[data-color-mode=
=3Ddark] [data-colorid=3Dlgxzoavn1p]{color:#cbd7ff}</style>During the boot =
<span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"5ebbbf93-1789-4330-9bdc-c=
d537fb1caae">process</span>, a boot menu is available on request. Through t=
his menu, you can start boot modes for troubleshooting. There are modes to =
access system parameters, or to reset the device to the factory defaults if=
 the device is configured incorrectly or if you experience problems when bo=
oting.</p>
<hr local-id=3D"0e7cc5aefe9f">
<p local-id=3D"c9ece69bd21b">=E2=86=92 During the boot process, press the [=
Esc] key repeatedly in rapid succession<span data-colorid=3D"bg9h8xzui6">&n=
bsp;</span>in the second stage loader, when the <code><span class=3D"inline=
-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"39fc234e-f1b1-4be3-8cf4-44f8b17537d7">loading =
kernel</span></code><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"39fc2=
34e-f1b1-4be3-8cf4-44f8b17537d7"> message is shown on the screen.</span><br=
>
The boot menu is displayed with the available boot modes:</p><span class=3D=
"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrapper confluence-embedded-ma=
nual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-content-image=
-border image-left" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"40862f0ae728114ff=
232fd7bfb7a9ef4cc55fb105274523e09e0ed4fb31bc531" data-image-src=3D"https://=
igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302494/OS12_Boot%20menu=
.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716364686026&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&=
amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"369" data-width=3D"436" data-unresolved-commen=
t-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73308675" data-linked-resource-ver=
sion=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-de=
fault-alias=3D"OS12_Boot menu.png" data-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlas=
sian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-=
resource-container-id=3D"73302494" data-linked-resource-container-version=
=3D"6" data-media-id=3D"21cd7e8e-66fd-4b9e-9e86-46cd2d192523" data-media-ty=
pe=3D"file" height=3D"396"></span>
<p local-id=3D"a67fdd09b5a8"></p>
<p local-id=3D"35015fa350ec">Using the arrow keys, navigate to one of the b=
oot modes and press the [Enter] key to start the process. You can start the=
 following boot modes:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"208d09854286">
<li local-id=3D"53db6033cc4a">
<p local-id=3D"17807316e935"><a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wik=
i/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302494/Boot+Menu+in+IGEL+OS+12#QuietBoot" r=
el=3D"nofollow"><strong>Quiet boot</strong></a>: Normal startup. (Default)<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"77ccaed100d8">
<p local-id=3D"15404a3dee1a"><a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wik=
i/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302494/Boot+Menu+in+IGEL+OS+12#VerboseBoot"=
 rel=3D"nofollow"><strong>Verbose boot</strong></a>: Start with system mess=
ages and an interactive root shell</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"706c2665d94a">
<p local-id=3D"3f95ba487e82"><a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wik=
i/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302494/Boot+Menu+in+IGEL+OS+12#VESABoot" re=
l=3D"nofollow"><strong><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"2d=
11e302-1829-4005-8aff-f160374f05c6">VESA only boot</span></strong></a><span=
 class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"2d11e302-1829-4005-8aff-f16037=
4f05c6">: </span><span data-colorid=3D"lgxzoavn1p"><span class=3D"inline-co=
mment-marker" data-ref=3D"2d11e302-1829-4005-8aff-f160374f05c6">Basic graph=
ic boot</span></span></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b37bde9bea3b">
<p local-id=3D"a9677a8c051e"><a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wik=
i/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302494/Boot+Menu+in+IGEL+OS+12#EmergencyBoo=
t" rel=3D"nofollow"><strong>Emergency boot (setup only)</strong></a>: Only =
the <strong>Setup </strong>window is available</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6603f9fd90d5">
<p local-id=3D"8f00ce2454a2"><a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wik=
i/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302494/Boot+Menu+in+IGEL+OS+12#FailsafeBoot=
" rel=3D"nofollow"><strong>Failsafe boot with CRC check</strong></a>: Start=
 with an integrity check of the operating system</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6d8f4ae967bd">
<p local-id=3D"0bcbe615c817"><a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wik=
i/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302494/Boot+Menu+in+IGEL+OS+12#ResetToFacto=
ry" rel=3D"nofollow"><strong>Reset to factory defaults</strong></a>: Reset =
the client to factory defaults</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fd685a25d53d">
<p local-id=3D"f2fce9f88460"><a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wik=
i/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302494/Boot+Menu+in+IGEL+OS+12#CustomBoot" =
rel=3D"nofollow"><strong>Custom boot command</strong></a>: Boot with config=
urable command line options</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"8e480c45c907" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-QuietBootQuietBoot">=
Quiet Boot<span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-Q=
uietBoot"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"QuietBoot"></span></=
span></h2>
<p local-id=3D"6c03a6eee772"><strong>Quiet boot</strong><span class=3D"lega=
cy-color-text-blue3">&nbsp;is the default boot mode. It is the normal start=
up mode. In this mode, all kernel messages are disabled and the graphical u=
ser interface is started.</span></p>
<h2 local-id=3D"c6eb82388842" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-VerboseBootVerboseBo=
ot">Verbose Boot<span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BootMenuinIGEL=
OS12-VerboseBoot"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"VerboseBoot"=
></span></span></h2>
<p local-id=3D"be7446d50abe">Unlike in&nbsp;<strong>Quiet boot</strong>&nbs=
p;mode, the kernel messages are shown in&nbsp;<strong>Verbose boot&nbsp;</s=
trong>mode. The boot process also pauses before the graphics system and the=
 user session start.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a4aeeb36946e">This gives you an opportunity to open a root s=
hell and interactively execute debugging commands (for example,&nbsp;<code>=
ifconfig</code>).</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-war=
ning">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-error confluence-inform=
ation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"c9c43ba67a15">Only use the root shell if you have adequate k=
nowledge of Linux or if you are instructed to do so by the IGEL Helpdesk an=
d are given appropriate guidance. Incorrect use can destroy the operating s=
ystem.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"747a7c4b9131"></p>
<p local-id=3D"a6abe3a0523c">To execute debugging commands:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"6f9cd83e27ce">
<li local-id=3D"b74caa67f615">
<p local-id=3D"8bebb68eac4e">Select&nbsp;<strong>Verbose boot</strong>&nbsp=
;from the boot menu.<br></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"019b0e19569a">
<p local-id=3D"125e840acd0f">Wait until the boot messages stop at&nbsp;<cod=
e>Reached target IGEL Network Online</code>.<br></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2f9116c336a1">
<p local-id=3D"0ccdefd0de23">Open a virtual console with one of the key com=
binations:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"97eb04d0cdbc">
<li local-id=3D"153230555bba">
<p local-id=3D"38258de68231">[Ctrl] + [Alt] + [F11]</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ac92ff228a76">
<p local-id=3D"8b6b27bab3ea">[Ctrl] + [Alt] + [F12]<br></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"3e8d3855a187">
<p local-id=3D"568c1f452a14">Log in by pressing [Return] and enter the root=
 password if necessary.<br></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8f5165c792b3">
<p local-id=3D"074844a85689">Go through the desired individual commands.<br=
></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0b004cc6a2c3">
<p local-id=3D"39d634973f99">Now enter the following command to continue th=
e normal boot process: <code>systemctl default</code><br>
The graphical user session starts.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"765cff7e5bb1" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-VESAOnlyBootVESABoot=
">VESA Only Boot<span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"BootMenuinIGEL=
OS12-VESABoot"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"VESABoot"></spa=
n></span></h2>
<p local-id=3D"385df1b3062e"><span data-colorid=3D"brq0eho2zs">Use this boo=
t mode if normal boot has graphic issues, for example, if the device has li=
mited Graphical Processor Unit (GPU) support. This mode is not manufacturer=
 specific. In this mode resolution and multimonitor mode and performance mi=
ght be limited.</span></p>
<h2 local-id=3D"c636226697c8" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-EmergencyBoot(SetupO=
nly)EmergencyBoot">Emergency Boot (Setup Only)<span class=3D"confluence-anc=
hor-link" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-EmergencyBoot"><span class=3D"confluence=
-anchor-link" id=3D"EmergencyBoot"></span></span></h2>
<p local-id=3D"97f2a38f8b3d">In the&nbsp;<strong>Emergency boot </strong>mo=
de, the device is started without network drivers and with a resolution of =
640 x 480 - 60 Hz. After the boot process, the <strong>Setup</strong> windo=
w is opened automatically.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c8ee01a89009">This mode is useful, for example, if you have =
selected an excessively high screen resolution or a wrong mouse type and th=
ese settings can no longer be changed in the normal setup. Unlike with a re=
set, the setup opens with the actual settings.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b2a6bb194e28">=E2=86=92 Once you are done with the changes, =
close the setup window to reboot the device.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"d64a6517b213" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-FailsafeBootwithCRCC=
heckFailsafeBoot">Failsafe Boot with CRC Check<span class=3D"confluence-anc=
hor-link" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-FailsafeBoot"><span class=3D"confluence-=
anchor-link" id=3D"FailsafeBoot"></span></span></h2>
<p local-id=3D"1b4572ec7e8c">During a&nbsp;<strong>Failsafe boot</strong>, =
a check of the file system is carried out first. Then, the&nbsp;<strong>Ver=
bose boot</strong> is started.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1fa014ae9caa">This mode is helpful if you no longer have a b=
ootable system after a firmware update. The&nbsp;<strong>Failsafe boot</str=
ong>&nbsp;checks where the problem is. If need be, an old version will be b=
ooted and you will need to repeat the firmware update.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"7596a4f630fa" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-ResettoFactoryDefaul=
tsResetToFactory">Reset to Factory Defaults<span class=3D"confluence-anchor=
-link" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-ResetToFactory"><span class=3D"confluence-a=
nchor-link" id=3D"ResetToFactory"></span></span></h2>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-war=
ning">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-error confluence-inform=
ation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"f5ca5292d809">If you select&nbsp;<strong>Reset to factory de=
faults</strong>, all personal settings on the device (including your passwo=
rd and the sessions you have configured) will be lost.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-tip=
">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-approve confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"417e914aab95">You can reset IGEL OS devices to factory defau=
lts through the boot menu, but the best practice is to reset devices using =
the OSC as descried in <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://kb.igel.c=
om/en/igel-os-base-system/current/how-to-deploy-igel-os-12-with-igel-os-cre=
ator-osc" rel=3D"nofollow">How to Deploy IGEL OS 12 with IGEL OS Creator (O=
SC)</a>.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b7611d333165">You can also reset your device to factory defa=
ults through the UMS Web App. In this case,&nbsp;the device will be removed=
 from the UMS and you will have to register your device with the UMS again.=
 For details, see<em> </em><a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://kb.ig=
el.com/en/universal-management-suite/current/how-to-reset-a-device-to-facto=
ry-defaults-via-the-" rel=3D"nofollow">How to Reset a Device to Factory Def=
aults via the IGEL UMS Web App</a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"5d132b625d33">Before the reset procedure is carried out:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"96874cf4f77f">
<li local-id=3D"a75a96260ac6">
<p local-id=3D"8f21bf336c57">Confirm the displayed warning message.<br></p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"dc277601675b">
<p local-id=3D"50487d0f1fad">If the device is protected by an administrator=
 password, enter the password. You have three attempts.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"35546a6f506d">The administrator password can be set or chang=
ed under <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://kb.igel.com/en/igel-os-=
base-system/current/password-and-user-types-in-igel-os-12" rel=3D"nofollow"=
><strong>Security &gt; Password &gt; Administrator</strong></a> using a pro=
file or the device configurator in the IGEL UMS Web App.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h2 local-id=3D"41e3aab33fcb" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-CustomBootCommandCus=
tomBoot">Custom Boot Command<span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"Bo=
otMenuinIGELOS12-CustomBoot"><span class=3D"confluence-anchor-link" id=3D"C=
ustomBoot"></span></span></h2>
<p local-id=3D"42dcd620399c">In the <strong>Custom boot command </strong>mo=
de, preconfigured options are placed on the kernel command line. This allow=
s you, for example, to investigate and rectify problems with specific hardw=
are components.</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-war=
ning">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-error confluence-inform=
ation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"db935e0d81a6">The <strong>Custom boot command</strong> is me=
rely a temporary solution =E2=80=93 it is not an everyday booting method. I=
t must therefore be selected manually in the boot menu.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"5a7585debe79"></p>
<p local-id=3D"d920200f0e7c">To configure the options for the <strong>Custo=
m boot command</strong>, proceed as follows:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"b46d1b13b957">
<li local-id=3D"f2ad34d4212d">
<p local-id=3D"c33d5a164331">Open a&nbsp;<span class=3D"inline-comment-mark=
er" data-ref=3D"2ff43774-085e-4b1e-8565-69e320faf08a">local terminal</span>=
&nbsp;and log in as&nbsp;<code>root</code>.<br></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1fbd5a8f8103">
<p local-id=3D"31dbd2ca9579">Enter the following command to bring up the cu=
rrent options:<br><code>bootreg get /dev/igfdisk boot_cmd</code><br></p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"2279908506fc">
<p local-id=3D"a968f81ada9f">Save your desired options with the following c=
ommand:<br><code>bootreg set /dev/igfdisk boot_cmd "&lt;Your Options&gt;"</=
code><br></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"97575150bba0">
<p local-id=3D"2f3a4f74b03c">Check the options that you have entered:<br><c=
ode>bootreg get /dev/igfdisk boot_cmd</code></p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"4dbdf88f028c">If you would like to delete options for the Cu=
stom boot command, leave an empty string of characters in their place:&nbsp=
;<code>bootreg set /dev/igfdisk boot_cmd ""</code></p>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"1462d1fae34d"></p>
<h2 local-id=3D"ff926327778e" id=3D"BootMenuinIGELOS12-IGELTechVideo">IGEL =
Tech Video</h2><iframe class=3D"youtube-player" type=3D"text/html" style=3D=
"width: 400px; height: 300px" src=3D"//www.youtube.com/embed/bpfWNIR6eUE?wm=
ode=3Dopaque" frameborder=3D"0"> </iframe>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p local-id=3D"010129a20582">In the video, IGEL OS11 is used for demonstrat=
ion.</p>
</div>
</div>
